==================================================
KEY POINTS TO REMEMBER
==================================================

1. Data preprocessing prepares raw data for ML.

2. Missing values must be handled before training when the
   chosen model/pipeline cannot accept them.

3. Duplicates can give repeated observations too much influence.

4. Outliers are unusually distant observations.

5. Categorical data must often be encoded into numerical form.

6. Label Encoding → categories become numbers.

7. One-Hot Encoding → each category becomes a binary column.

8. Standardization → mean ≈ 0 and standard deviation ≈ 1.

9. Normalization → commonly scales values to 0–1.

10. Feature Selection → select existing useful features.

11. Feature Extraction → create a new representation/features.

12. Feature Engineering → create/transform features to improve
    their usefulness to the model.